From 03d588e42721b8449b6b7afdc8f4f96fbe21ad60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:30:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] Test the verifier authority on real contracts over a
 canonical-trie chain

The rig can run on a pinned reth --dev chain (RIG_CHAIN_NODE=reth; chain id 8453
genesis, datadir in /tmp, proof window 1024) because anvil keeps zero-valued
storage slots as trie leaves, which the verifier rightly refuses. On reth the
deployment snapshot, host admission with catalog moderation, settlement reads,
tampered or missing witnesses and a stale head all behave as specified; on anvil
reads of zero-writing contracts are asserted to refuse.

(cherry picked from commit 0c43e4db89f1be615ff11319abc43aefd69a9fcb)
